Formal Definition of a Finite Automata A finite automata can be formally denoted by a five-tuple ( Q, Σ, δ, q0, F ) where Q →  set of states Σ → input alphabet δ → transition function : Q X ∑ → Q q0 → initial state F → set of final states, , F ⊆Q Formal definition of this automata is ( { q0, q1, q2, q3 }, { a, b }, δ, q0, {q2} ) where δ is defined as δ ( q0 , a ) = q1 δ ( q0 , b ) = q3 δ ( q1 , a ) = q1 δ ( q1 , b ) = q2 δ ( q2 , a ) = q1 δ ( q2 , b ) = q2 δ ( q3 , a ) = q3 δ ( q3 , b ) = q3 EXAMPLE

