Acceptance of input strings by NFA • An input string will be accepted by a NFA if there is at least one path that ends in a final state • The language accepted by a NFA is the set of all strings accepted by the NFA Example:

Check whether the string 00111 is accepted by the NFA given below.  Also find the language accepted by the NFA.

Language Accepted by the NFA Set of all binary strings with any number of 0s followed by any number of 1s Acceptance of string δ ( q0 , 00111 )  = δ ( { q0 , q1 } , 0111 ) = δ ( { q0 , q1 } , 111 ) = δ ( { q1 , q2 } , 11 ) = δ ( { q1 , q2 } , 1 ) = { q1 , q2 }

